      "totalDuration": "1 yr 8 mos",
      "description": "Rapidly promoted to a role with increasing responsibilities based on exceptional teamwork, productivity and technology skills that streamlined processes and improved productivity. Develop top-quality code on tight deadlines as an integral part of a development team working in ambitious deadlines. Primary focus on the in-house, customized Manufacturing Execution System (MES), Scrap Management Tool, Modular Class-based design and the Pick-to-Light (P2L) system as an integral part of a dynamic 5-member team. \n\nLeverage knowledge of Python, JavaScript, jQuery, CSS, HTML, Django, SQL and Microsoft SQL Server to deliver projects on time and on budget, and to achieve strategic goals for the organization. \n\nAccelerated delivery of the MES project after being assigned to the team as a subject matter expert, 6 months into a 2-year project with a team that was struggling to meet timelines.\n\nRapidly responded to a series of 6 redesigns and wide-spread changes in product requirements over 2-3 months, taking on extra responsibility for development to deliver the MES project on time. \n\nConcurrently provided support for code in an interim QA role while serving as a lead developer.\n\nSingle-handedly developed the front end of the Scrap Management Tool to deliver the project on time, in just 4 days, to wide-spread acclaim. \n\nVolunteered to modulate code for the EMS, accelerating delivery of dynamical configuration project without customized code and facilitating faster development on future operations, on time and on budget.\n\nIncreased employee morale and boosted productivity to 150% by developing a customized P2L (Pick-to-Light) system with a two-part service handler sending and receiving commands asynchronously.",
