      "totalDuration": "1 yr 10 mos",
      "description": "Quickly assimilated new information to become a top-performing contributor to the 5-member Solutions team, autonomously prioritizing tasks to deliver project segments on time and on budget. Developed extensive skills in troubleshooting new and legacy code for the Energy Management and Control System (EMS), Management Downtime Tracking System (MDTS) and Manufacturing Execution System (MES).\n\nUtilized Python, JavaScript, jQuery, CSS, HTML, Django, SQL, Microsoft SQL Server, PostgreSQL, and Linux along with Amazon AWS, SES and EC2 Services to deliver against overarching objectives. \n\nImproved web user interface (UI) in first 6 months by redesigning the client-side code with improvements on navigation, visual ascetics, functionality, scripting performance and customization options.\n\nElevated team productivity by stepping up as the primary developer for the EMS project, single-handedly refactoring ~70% of the code base to improve readability and boost overall system performance.\n\nImproved code modularity for web page handler, eliminating redundancy to reduce code by ~30%; streamlined PTAC configuration data logic to reduce EMS runtime ~20%. \n\nTransformed downtime tracking and improved productivity by developing, testing and troubleshooting a flexible system using multiple interfaces including mobile devices for the MDTS in just 3 months. \n\nAchieved 83%+ performance improvement by rebuilding an email service from the ground up to deliver results in 20 minutes vs. 2 hours while reducing resource load.",
